{"step_index":83,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T14:55:41Z","thinking":"**Investigating Empty Match Reasons**\n\nThe script produced empty matches because it searched only within the file content, not the filenames themselves. The intended records were present as filenames: `history/releases/record-b9a1361197.md` and `history/support/record-0131162d69.md`.\n\nNow, searching for all occurrences of those record IDs (`b9a1361197`, `0131162d69`), as well as other potential search terms (`August 30`, `September`, `mobile`), is warranted.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c '\nimport os, glob\n\nkeywords = [\"September\", \"mobile\", \"Android\", \"phone\", \"draft\", \"waiting\", \"quiet digest\", \"Sunday Room\", \"Focus Shelf\", \"status filter\"]\nmatches = {k: set() for k in keywords}\n\nfor root, _, files in os.walk(\"/workspace/product\"):\n    for f in files:\n        path = os.path.join(root, f)\n        try:\n            with open(path) as fp:\n                text = fp.read()\n                for k in keywords:\n                    if k.lower() in text.lower():\n                        matches[k].add(os.path.relpath(path, \"/workspace/product\"))\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n\nfor k, v in matches.items():\n    print(f\"=== {k} ({len(v)} files) ===\")\n    # if fewer than 15 files, print them\n    if len(v) < 15:\n        for p in sorted(v):\n            print(f\"  {p}\")\n    else:\n        # print non-operations / non-support if lots\n        special = [p for p in v if not p.startswith(\"history/operations\") and not p.startswith(\"history/evidence\") and not p.startswith(\"history/actions\")]\n        print(f\"  Top special: {special}\")\n'","Cwd":"/workspace","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Searching keywords in product dir","toolSummary":"Keyword search across product directory"}}]}
